From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:05:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 003/117] nvme-pci: Add Apple ANS FlatDMA support

Apple ANS exposes NVMe queues over PCI but requires a proprietary
command flag, a loader-provided host-memory buffer and FlatDMA request
mappings.

Add private nvme-pci DMA hooks and keep the controller-specific logic
in separate glue. Reinitialize the HMB and invalidate every FlatDMA
slot whenever nvme-pci enables the controller so reset_controller can
rebuild the controller state.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
[Orchard: ported to v7.3-rc1. The structures moved to pci-internal.h keep
 mainline's __guarded_by(&sq_lock) annotations on struct nvme_queue, and
 the Makefile keeps CONTEXT_ANALYSIS. The FlatDMA code does not access the
 guarded fields.]

Orchard-replay-of: 599f994728d77940ba3c90a1d19d28c28c48844e
